A||||1||c0rrigan||Fuel injection swap?||||5||
Z||000000||c0rrigan||05-17-2000||10:40 PM||||I've got an '84 2M4 in which I swapped the 4 banger for a 1980 carburated 2.8L.  I now have the opportunity to pick up an 85 SE with V6 that has a cracked block, but the upper portion of the engine is fine.  My question is this:  Can I transplant the heads/intake/electronics from the SE to my carburated engine.  I believe that the block is the same.  I assume I may also have to change the pushrods, and possibly the camshaft.  As long as I can use my block, I don't see this being too difficult a job.<P>Also, the seats are in almost perfect condition.  Talk about something rare!  Almost makes it worth buying just for the seats.<P>Any opinions?||||reg||5
Z||000001||mwbackus||05-18-2000||12:48 PM||||Sounds like a good plan to me.  Very few of the 80's carbed engines had the HO heads, so it would be a performance upgrade just bolting the Fiero 2.8 heads on.  The cam and oil pump would would also need an upgrade to equal the stock Fiero 2.8's.  I would suggest just building it to a stroked 3.2 using the Fiero FI, etc..  There is lots of info on doing the 3.2 build here on the forum, just do some searching.<P>Mike B.||||reg||1
